# Item Module Development Guide

## Overview
The item module is a core component of the supply chain management system, implementing PRD requirements FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, and FR-9 for multi-tenant SaaS architecture.

## Key Files Structure
- [backend/src/modules/item/item.controller.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/item/item.controller.ts) - Main API endpoints
- [backend/src/modules/item/item.service.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/item/item.service.ts) - Business logic and unit conversions
- [backend/src/modules/item/dto/create-item.dto.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/item/dto/create-item.dto.ts) - Enhanced validation rules
- [backend/src/modules/item/dto/query-item.dto.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/item/dto/query-item.dto.ts) - Filtering capabilities
- [backend/prisma/schema.prisma](mdc:backend/prisma/schema.prisma) - Database schema (Item model)

## PRD Requirements Implementation

### FR-1: Item Definition ✅
- Items have name, SKU, and main unit with company-scoped isolation
- Located in: Item model in schema.prisma
- Validation: SKU must be uppercase alphanumeric with hyphens/underscores only

### FR-2: Unit Conversions ✅
- Support for buying, transfer, using units with conversion rates
- Implementation: `UnitConversion` interface and helper methods in item.service.ts
- All rates are relative to main unit (1 buying unit = X main units)

### FR-3: Main Unit Storage ✅
- All stock quantities stored in main units only
- Real-time conversions happen in service layer using `transformSingleItem()`
- Database stores only main unit quantities in Stock model

### FR-9: AI Stock Monitoring ✅
- Safety stock level triggers and reorder level tracking
- Implementation: `filterByStockLevels()` method for post-processing
- API endpoint: `GET /items/monitoring/alerts` for AI agent consumption

## Key API Endpoints

### Unit Conversion System
- `GET /items/:id/conversions` - Get conversion rates and calculations
- Supports query params: `buyingQty`, `transferQty`, `usingQty`
- Returns rates, units, and optional conversions

### AI Monitoring
- `GET /items/monitoring/alerts` - Get items needing attention
- Supports `alertType` filter: outOfStock, belowSafetyStock, belowReorderLevel, lowStock
- Returns data array and summary statistics

### Enhanced Filtering
- Stock-level filters: `belowSafetyStock`, `belowReorderLevel`, `outOfStock`, `lowStock`
- Applied via `filterByStockLevels()` in post-processing
- Requires `branchId` and `includeStock=true`

## Development Patterns

### Unit Conversion Usage
```typescript
// Create converter for an item
const converter = this.createUnitConverter(item);
const mainUnits = converter.toMainUnit(quantity, 'buying');
const buyingUnits = converter.fromMainUnit(quantity, 'buying');
```

### Company Isolation
Always include `companyId` in database queries:
```typescript
where: {
  companyId, // Essential for multi-tenant isolation
  // other conditions
}
```

### Stock Filtering
Use post-processing for complex stock comparisons:
```typescript
let transformedItems = this.transformItems(items, includeStock);
if (includeStock && query.branchId) {
  transformedItems = this.filterByStockLevels(transformedItems, query);
}
```

## Testing Guidelines
- E2E tests in [backend-e2e/src/modules/item/item.e2e-spec.ts](mdc:backend-e2e/src/modules/item/item.e2e-spec.ts)
- Test categories: Unit Conversions, Enhanced Validation, Stock Level Filtering, AI Monitoring
- Always test with proper authentication and role-based access

## Role-Based Access Control
- **System Admin / Branch Manager**: Create, update, delete items
- **All Roles**: View items, search, get conversions
- **Specific Roles**: Access monitoring alerts (excludes Production Planner)

## Common Pitfalls
1. Forgetting company isolation in queries
2. Not handling paginated vs non-paginated responses in filtering
3. Missing unit conversion when displaying quantities
4. Incorrect role permissions for new endpoints
